    ],
    "word_count": 52,
    "html": "<p>Hubert Freidl is an Austrian businessman who led Lyoness and myWorld, developing an international network of merchants and shoppers. Born in Graz and trained in wholesale trade, he worked in insurance and software before building the shopping-rewards business. He subsequently established Salters Advisory in Dubai, advising founders on business structure and expansion.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "At Lyoness, Hubert Freidl promoted a shopping community organised around a cashback card. Customers received money back when buying from participating merchants, while the network linked businesses across national borders. The company also allocated a share of purchases to its Child & Family Foundation.\n\nFreidl took part in the opening of the rebuilt Nelson Mandela No-Moscow Primary School in Qunu, South Africa, alongside members of Mandela's family in 2013. Foundation donors financed the school's continuing support. Returning in 2018, he joined its director and the headteacher in dedicating the school to long-standing supporter Gerry Seebacher. Pupils received bags containing school supplies.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 86,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Primary historical operating account and complete foundation event report establish the specific mechanisms and his participation."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S4",
      "S9"
    ],
    "word_count": 100,
    "html": "<p>At Lyoness, Hubert Freidl promoted a shopping community organised around a cashback card. Customers received money back when buying from participating merchants, while the network linked businesses across national borders. The company also allocated a share of purchases to its Child &amp; Family Foundation.</p>\r\n<p>Freidl took part in the opening of the rebuilt Nelson Mandela No-Moscow Primary School in Qunu, South Africa, alongside members of Mandela's family in 2013. Foundation donors financed the school's continuing support. Returning in 2018, he joined its director and the headteacher in dedicating the school to long-standing supporter Gerry Seebacher. Pupils received bags containing school supplies.</p>\r\n"
  },
